# PART VIII — MANDATORY IMPLEMENTATION ORDER

## 22. Complete All Functional Work First

Implement the project in the following sequence.

### Phase 1: Audit and planning
Inspect the repository, identify existing functionality, and prepare the implementation plan.

### Phase 2: Campaign system
Expand industry coverage, implement campaign management, and build the ICP and advanced-filter functionality.

### Phase 3: Prospect intelligence
Implement or improve discovery, research, source evidence, qualification, and persistent prospect records.

### Phase 4: LinkedIn messaging
Implement the canonical template, three observation alternatives, evidence display, message comparison, editing, and copying.

### Phase 5: Gmail integration
Implement OAuth, secure credential handling, real Gmail draft creation, draft management, and error recovery.

### Phase 6: Unified workflow
Connect campaigns, research, qualification, LinkedIn messages, Gmail drafts, and status tracking.

### Phase 7: Functional verification
Test the entire workflow, fix integration problems, verify database persistence, and confirm that existing functionality remains intact.

### Mandatory gate before redesign

**Do not begin the visual redesign until all preceding functional phases have been implemented, integrated, and tested to the extent possible in the available environment.**

If external credentials are unavailable, complete the integration code, test what can be tested, and document the exact external setup still required.

Do not confuse missing external configuration with completed production verification.

At this point, the functional version must be stable enough that the visual redesign can proceed without changing the underlying business logic.

